.TH L10N-LINT 1 "February 2026" "l10n-lint 1.15.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
l10n\-lint \- lint and validate PO/XLIFF/TS translation files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B l10n\-lint
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBl10n\-lint\fR checks translation files (PO, XLIFF, TS) for common
errors such as missing format specifiers, inconsistent punctuation,
untranslated entries, overly long translations, encoding issues, and
more. It can scan local files, directories (recursively), or fetch
files directly from GitHub repositories.
.PP
By default, l10n\-lint outputs a human\-readable text report. Use
\fB\-\-format\fR to switch to JSON, HTML, GitHub Actions annotations,
or GNU/Emacs\-compatible output.
.PP
Exit codes: 0 = no errors, 1 = errors found, 2 = usage error.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PATHS
Files or directories to lint. When directories are given, l10n\-lint
searches recursively for .po, .xliff, and .ts files (unless
\fB\-\-no\-recursive\fR is set). If omitted, reads from the current
directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-github\fR \fIREPO\fR
Lint a GitHub repository directly. Accepts \fIowner/repo\fR or a full
GitHub URL. The repository is cloned to a temporary directory and
scanned for translation files. Combine with \fB\-\-path\fR to limit
the search scope.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR
Path filter within a GitHub repository. Only files under this path are
linted. For example, \fB\-\-github user/repo \-\-path po/\fR limits
scanning to the \fIpo/\fR directory. Has no effect on local paths.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format. Choices: \fBtext\fR (default, human\-readable),
\fBjson\fR (structured output for scripting), \fBhtml\fR (standalone
HTML report), \fBgithub\fR (GitHub Actions annotation format for CI),
\fBgnu\fR (Emacs\-compatible file:line:col format).
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Save the report to a file instead of printing to stdout. Useful with
\fB\-\-format html\fR for generating reports.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-length\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum allowed translation length in characters. Translations exceeding
this limit trigger a warning. Default: 500.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-recursive\fR
Do not descend into subdirectories when scanning. Only files directly
in the given paths are linted.
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Treat warnings as errors. With this flag, warnings cause a non\-zero
exit code. Useful for CI pipelines that require zero warnings.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Show only a summary (total files, errors, warnings). Individual issue
details are suppressed.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Exit code only — produce no output at all. Designed for CI integration
where only the exit code matters.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-fuzzy\fR
Do not warn about fuzzy (unreviewed) translations.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show detailed progress information, including each file being scanned.
.TP
\fB\-G\fR, \fB\-\-gtk\fR
Launch the GTK4/Adwaita graphical interface instead of running in
CLI mode. Requires \fBl10n\-lint\-gtk\fR to be installed.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version number and exit.
.SH CHECKS PERFORMED
l10n\-lint performs the following checks on each translation entry:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFormat specifiers\fR — verifies that printf\-style (%s, %d, %1$s)
and Python\-style ({0}, {name}) placeholders match between source and
translation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPunctuation\fR — checks that trailing punctuation (periods, colons,
ellipsis) is consistent between source and translation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLeading/trailing whitespace\fR — flags mismatched whitespace.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAccelerator keys\fR — ensures &\- or _\-style keyboard accelerators
are preserved.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBXML/HTML tags\fR — verifies that markup tags in the source appear
in the translation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEmpty translations\fR — warns about msgid entries with empty msgstr.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFuzzy entries\fR — warns about unreviewed fuzzy translations (unless
\fB\-\-skip\-fuzzy\fR is used).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOverly long translations\fR — flags translations exceeding
\fB\-\-max\-length\fR characters.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEncoding issues\fR — detects invalid UTF\-8 sequences.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No errors found.
.TP
.B 1
One or more errors found (or warnings, if \fB\-\-strict\fR is used).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (invalid arguments, file not found).
.SH EXAMPLES
Lint all PO files in the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
l10n\-lint .
.fi
.RE
.PP
Lint a GitHub repository:
.PP
.RS
.nf
l10n\-lint \-\-github yeager/ubuntu\-l10n \-\-path po/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate an HTML report:
.PP
.RS
.nf
l10n\-lint \-\-format html \-\-output report.html po/
.fi
.RE
.PP
CI integration (strict, no output):
.PP
.RS
.nf
l10n\-lint \-\-check \-\-strict .
.fi
.RE
